\contentsline {deleted}{Deleted: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{cooperative yield}}{2}{section*.8}%
\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{Wait; this is an external result, not a required outcome of the Silo port}}{2}{section*.9}%
\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{The midpoint uses saved Mac/emulated-Linux evidence because a working UINTR host was not secured. The guest and prior AWS VM report UINTR=0; these results apply to those environments. PACE has no usable interface available to the team. Qualify each alternative independently before claiming access.}}{2}{section*.10}%
\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{Pursue an approved Intel cloud or physical host; verify exposure, interface permission and actual delivery. The authors' artifact may provide a separately labeled reference run on a qualified host. If the November 8 access checkpoint fails, consult staff; retain native UINTR as the final objective unless a scope change is approved.}}{3}{section*.11}%
\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{Retain the documented q2\_min\_stock\_v1 Silo projection and checksum oracle. Measure reads/runtime on the eventual native host before setting scale and intervals; no unsupported 140-microsecond estimate or claimed millisecond runtime is used. Record all departures from the paper.}}{3}{section*.12}%
\contentsline {deleted}{Deleted: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{10,000}}{4}{section*.13}%
\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{$N$ completed record reads, with $N=64$ for the archived smoke. Test the paper's 10,000 on the final workload and report observed checkpoints rather than assuming they occur.}}{4}{section*.14}%
\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{Use open-loop arrivals and explicit outcomes. Keep per-run quantiles and counts; never average quantiles. Any pooled summary must identify its exact cohorts. Retain low-sample tail flags, retries, rejections, cancellation and cutoff/drain accounting. Match all policies on one qualified host before the native comparison.}}{4}{section*.15}%
\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{Voluntary contexts and protected regions precede native delivery/switching. The glibc voluntary ABI tests do not validate interrupt-time state. Native I12--I17 acceptance gates remain mandatory.}}{4}{section*.16}%
\contentsline {deleted}{Deleted: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{The Linux-signal backend is not yet built.}}{4}{section*.17}%
\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{It is locally implemented and tested for restricted audited windows. Signal batching/starvation repetitions are complete locally. Model events use checkpoint service and remain separate from real handlers/captures; neither substitutes for native UINTR delivery or native performance.}}{4}{section*.18}%
\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{Target Figure 10-style matched Wait, Cooperative and native Preemptive runs after correctness gates, then confirm additional coverage against the final rubric. Record host limits versus the paper's 16-worker setup, queue capacities, intervals, duration and core placement. Defer adaptive thresholds, architecture and distributed extensions.}}{4}{section*.19}%
